(6981082, 1053309, 77196, '<td valign="top">Never understood why this doesn''t relate to folks. <br/> <br/>For me, the path has always had strong meaning - a metaphor for the course of one''s life, the result(s) of a choice, walking alone, walking with others, overcoming difficulty or discomfort (like walking barefoot through the snow), etc. <br/> <br/>I especially like the "contrarian" shadows of branches crossing the path.<br/></td>', 'Never understood why this doesn''t relate to folks.  For me, the path has always had strong meaning - a metaphor for the course of one''s life, the result(s) of a choice, walking alone, walking with others, overcoming difficulty or discomfort (like walking barefoot through the snow), etc.  I especially like the "contrarian" shadows of branches crossing the path.', '2013-02-18 11:17:03.000000', NULL, 0),
