(6981232, 1053216, 135629, '<td valign="top">Thanks for your comment! And you are right they wouldn''t move :) <br/> <br/>As for the votes I got...  Yeah, product folks and those who have not shot motor-sports sometimes tend to forget that you can''t always just move your lamps around, slide the table over, stand around and give some thought, change the entire background, adjust a bunch of stuff, think about it some more, etc.... when you are shooting the individual split seconds of professional racing :) Racing is busy! If it wasn''t I assume it wouldn''t exist any more. As for the challenge entry criteria, I believe I followed all of the <i><u>very detailed and specific criteria</u></i> for this specific challenge precisely :) "Take a photograph where the subject relates to milk or milk products." It''s always funny how people perceive and box themselves in, when all that was asked was that it''s a photo relating to milk or milk products. Any further guidance is lore :) <br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by dtremain:</b></div><hr/><i> Guess now you know why not. I really like this shot - truck is sharp, wheels blurred, dust kicking up. And yes, it is busy, but I''m guessing you wouldn''t have much success trying to get all the folks to move their rigs... ;-p </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Thanks for your comment! And you are right they wouldn''t move :)  As for the votes I got...  Yeah, product folks and those who have not shot motor-sports sometimes tend to forget that you can''t always just move your lamps around, slide the table over, stand around and give some thought, change the entire background, adjust a bunch of stuff, think about it some more, etc.... when you are shooting the individual split seconds of professional racing :) Racing is busy! If it wasn''t I assume it wouldn''t exist any more. As for the challenge entry criteria, I believe I followed all of the very detailed and specific criteria for this specific challenge precisely :) "Take a photograph where the subject relates to milk or milk products." It''s always funny how people perceive and box themselves in, when all that was asked was that it''s a photo relating to milk or milk products. Any further guidance is lore :)  Originally posted by dtremain: Guess now you know why not. I really like this shot - truck is sharp, wheels blurred, dust kicking up. And yes, it is busy, but I''m guessing you wouldn''t have much success trying to get all the folks to move their rigs... ;-p ', '2013-02-18 15:54:45.000000', NULL, 0),
